1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,055
Meet Claro, banking support in Spanish and Portuguese, with no language or
profile setup.

2
00:00:06,055 --> 00:00:10,174
These screenshots show actual local test runs with team authored fixtures.

3
00:00:10,174 --> 00:00:15,945
The customer opens the chat immediately. The service keeps a trusted, isolated
demo identity.

4
00:00:16,845 --> 00:00:22,488
The same customer moves from Spanish to Portuguese without changing identity
or selecting a language.

5
00:00:22,488 --> 00:00:29,069
Claro identifies the transaction from the conversation, asking for
clarification when the reference is ambiguous.

6
00:00:29,069 --> 00:00:36,010
The authorized record shows one hundred twenty nine thousand Colombian pesos
as pending, with its source and historical date.

7
00:00:36,910 --> 00:00:40,754
The customer reports an unfamiliar Tienda charge after a phone call.

8
00:00:40,754 --> 00:00:50,975
Before creating the case, the confirmation shows the attached transaction: T X
E S one zero two, one hundred twenty nine thousand Colombian pesos, pending.

9
00:00:50,975 --> 00:00:59,563
It keeps the customer report separate from verified record facts. A separate
confirmation creates the case; typing yes in chat cannot execute it.

10
00:00:59,563 --> 00:01:05,933
An explicit general request for an analyst attaches no transaction. No refund
or card blocking is promised.

11
00:01:06,833 --> 00:01:11,161
Every successful case creation needs a committed record and verified read
back.

12
00:01:11,161 --> 00:01:15,255
Retries keep the same idempotency key and stop after three attempts.

13
00:01:15,255 --> 00:01:18,397
A verification failure never becomes a success claim.

14
00:01:19,297 --> 00:01:22,721
The analyst workspace asks a specific follow up question.

15
00:01:22,721 --> 00:01:26,889
The customer opens that saved question and answers with the same chat
composer.

16
00:01:26,889 --> 00:01:29,951
A verified reply returns the case to the review queue.

17
00:01:30,851 --> 00:01:35,749
The analyst sees the original report, the question, and the customer reply in
order.

18
00:01:35,749 --> 00:01:39,658
After closing the review, reloading reads the four persisted events.

19
00:01:39,658 --> 00:01:44,778
Customer chat and reviewer links replace profile selection. The backend owns
the history.

20
00:01:45,678 --> 00:01:50,940
One FastAPI service owns sessions, scoped tools, and transactional case
storage.

21
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:55,043
Jev routing and DeepSeek Flash wording are implemented behind bounded
adapters.

22
00:01:55,043 --> 00:02:01,363
Live inference still requires explicit authorization for metered use. These
captures used local processing.

23
00:02:01,363 --> 00:02:10,139
Provider status and fallback are disclosed. Only entered sandbox messages and
minimized fixture context may leave; organizer data never does.

24
00:02:11,039 --> 00:02:15,269
Language understanding and complete workflow outcomes are evaluated
separately.

25
00:02:15,269 --> 00:02:22,607
The same authored workloads compare the baseline and proposed system. Current
reruns are regression evidence, with failures preserved.

26
00:02:22,607 --> 00:02:28,507
Authored scenarios and mocked provider tests do not prove real customer
performance or live provider quality.

27
00:02:29,407 --> 00:02:36,107
The fraud candidates did not pass the validation promotion gate. These public
fixtures receive no fraud probability.

28
00:02:36,107 --> 00:02:38,650
The customer report still reaches human review.

29
00:02:38,650 --> 00:02:50,281
Claro completes a bilingual conversation and verified follow up, with explicit
limits and reproducible evidence. Real banking requires approved identity,
policies, and durable storage.
